00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:09.589 align:start position:0%
 
hello  good morning again  the uh  committee meeting is being live streamed  so very minds that anything can be seen  after  so so this is the uh decision of the  subcommittee  the committee has considered all written  evidence and the representation  representations made at the hearing an  additional written representation  received from the interested party who  was unable to attend the meeting  in the hearing today the committee has  also considered the step  set the steps set out on page  4.21 which the applicants will take in  order to promote the four licensing  objectives  the condition are as follows  which again is the principle of  prevention of crime and disorders  the premises license holder will  maintain a digital cctv system that  covers the premises including the main  area which will be used for display of  alcohol  the cctv images will be retained for 31  days a member of the management team  will be on the premises at the times the  store is open  and will be the initial point of contact  for any issues that may arise  public safety the premises license  holder will maintain  policies and procedures in  relation to relevant obligations and  legislation these will be available upon  request  prevention of public nuisance the  premises will demonstrate a good  neighbor ethos and  that they play an attractive part in the  local community  protection and protection of child  children from harm the premises will  operate i think 25 policy the checkouts  will be programmed to prompt the  customer assistant when an alcohol  product is scanned at the checkout to  follow the thing 25 policy  all colleagues will receive training in  relation to the underlying  law policy systems and procedures this  training will be documented and  refresher training will be provided on a  regular basis  these will be available  upon request  the committee has carefully considered  the concerns raised by the interested  party relating to the license objectives  of prevention of public nuisance however  the committee is mindful of the fact  that no representations representations  have been made by essex police and  environmental health  the committee has taken into  consideration the applicant's verbal  representations relating to their  experience of running similar premises  elsewhere and its commitment to work  with local residents the committee is  satisfied that the concerns  of the interested party related to noise  will be addressed by the applicant  the committee has resolved to grant the  premises license subject to the usual  the usual mandatory conditions and the  additional conditions already included  above this concludes the hearing thank  you for attending have a nice afternoon  thank you  thank you

